WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
Treating Parkinson's disease
with... velvet beans.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.720
I have several videos on
foods that may trigger

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.200
Parkinson’s disease, but how
can diet be used in treatment?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.189
This video and the next look at
beans for treating this disease.

00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:25.496
"Can Velvet Beans or Fava Beans
Help Treat Parkinson’s Disease?"

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.640
Two centuries have passed
since James Parkinson’s Essay

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.240
on the Shaking Palsy described
a disease characterized

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.040
by tremor and problems
with movement.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.520
Today, treatment options
include surgically

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.560
implanting electrodes
into the brain.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.840
There has to be a better way.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.800
We’ve known since the 1950’s
that Parkinson’s disease

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.560
is manifested by a dopamine
deficiency in the brain.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.920
Well then why not
eat a dopamine diet?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.600
A variety of fruits
and vegetables contain

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.000
the same dopamine
made by our brain.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.200
Unfortunately, dopamine can’t
cross the blood-brain barrier

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.400
and hence is ineffective as therapy,
however the dopamine precursor,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.440
known as l-dopa or levodopa can
get from the blood up into the brain

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.160
where it can then be converted
to dopamine within the brain

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.880
by an enzyme called
decarboxylase.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.000
We don’t want the levodopa
to be converted to dopamine

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.480
outside the brain because
then it can’t get in,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.240
so we give people a decarboxylase
inhibitor which itself

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.000
can’t get into the brain, so that
keeps levodopa from prematurely

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.920
turning into dopamine before it
gets into the brain where we need it.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.320
So eating dopamine-
rich foods doesn’t help,

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.680
but what if we ate
levodopa-rich foods?

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.000
More than 1500 years before
Dr. Parkinson came on the scene,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.880
an Indian physician
seems to have nailed it

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.360
and even suggested a
treatment, velvet beans,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.320
the plant with the
highest amount of L-DOPA.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.400
Hmm, so might
there be a way to

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.960
forestall the epidemic
of Parkinson’s Disease

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.000
through plant-based
remedies after all?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.080
Levodopa is the gold standard
therapy for Parkinson’s patients,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.720
but most Parkinson’s
patients in low-income areas

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.440
cannot afford long-term
daily Levodopa therapy.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.320
In rural Africa, for example,
it is estimated that

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.440
only 15% of patients are
treated with levodopa,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.520
because the daily cost of Levodopa
treatment is about a dollar day,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.960
which may be half of
what people make in a day.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.760
Same with other regions
in the Global South.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.280
L-DOPA is mostly
unavailable or unaffordable.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.320
So patients frequently
use powdered velvet beans

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.200
as a replacement or
supplement to the drug.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.560
But does it work?
You never know...

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.280
until you put it to the test.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.480
Velvet beans in Parkinson’s
Disease a randomized,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.840
double blind, clinical study,
and, a dose of 30g,

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.920
which is about three tablespoons
led to a reliable and sustained

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.040
antiparkinsonian effect
in all patients,

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.160
working significantly
quicker than the drug,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.200
working significantly
longer than the drug,

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.160
and working significantly
better than the drug,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.640
in another double-blind, randomized,
head-to-head crossover study.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.360
The levodopa in velvet beans
appears to be 2–3 times

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.520
more potent as compared to the
same dose of pill-form Levodopa,

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.160
suspected to be because
there may be some intrinsic

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.240
decarboxylase inhibitor
compound in the plant as well.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.800
OK, but those were
single dose studies.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.640
What about the chronic use of
velvet beans for Parkinson’s.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.280
Fourteen patients with
advanced Parkinson’s received

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.480
roasted velvet bean powder
or the standard drug,

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.520
switching back and forth for
months, looking at changes

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.000
in quality of life,
activities of daily living,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.840
movement and
non-movement symptoms,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.440
and time with good mobility

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.640
without troublesome involuntary
writhing movements

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.840
and the velvet beans seemed
to work as well as the drug

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.600
in all measures of efﬁcacy,
including quality of life.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.440
Here’s a video of someone with
Parkinson’s solely treated with

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:07.040
velvet bean powder for 14 years,
before and after treatment:

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:13.440
Okay, can you put both
hands out for me?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.080
And tap your fingers on
the right, just the right.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:27.760
And the left...

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.120
And turn...

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:47.120
Now open and close..&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.880
the left,

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.360
the right...

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.840
turn, turn around

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.280
Despite the efficacy, the chances
of this cheap herbal remedy

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:15.600
ever being licensed seems
unlikely—and for good reason.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:19.520
First of all, the stuff
evidently tastes nasty.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.680
And we don’t really
have good data

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.920
going out more
than a few months.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.880
While velvet beans may
potentially be part of the answer

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.320
to Parkinson's
disease management

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:31.520
in low-income countries,
in high-income countries,

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.080
one may be tempted
to prefer them to drugs

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.800
just because it's a
"more natural therapy,"

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.440
but researchers discourage
patients and physicians

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.240
to consider its use when
the drugs are available.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.560
So levodopa in pill
form should remain

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.880
the first-line treatment
for Parkinson’s.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.760
However, velvet bean powder
may be better tolerated

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.040
in certain patients.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.600
Psychologically, some patients
just have a thing against

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.440
taking pills and so if they refuse,

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.920
then certainly the
beans can step in.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.640
But otherwise, velvet bean
supplements suffer from

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:03.840
the issues common to all
supplements, specifically lack

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.800
of sufficient regulation
and quality control.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.040
There’s all sorts of brands
out there, but there's no

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.600
head-to-head comparisons
as to which is best,

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.320
and the quality of the
products likely vary,

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.920
but you don’t know...

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.680
until you put it to the test.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.320
Six brands of velvet
bean product

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.800
were ordered through the
internet and most of them

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.840
four out of six showed a
large discrepancy between

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:31.440
the claim on their label and
the actual L-Dopa content,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:33.600
and only two even came close.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.240
The remaining products
contained considerably less,

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.960
less than 10% in two cases.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.640
Too bad there isn’t a food source
of L-dopa that you could just eat

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.040
instead of taking in a supplement.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.480
Well, wait a second.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.680
L-dopa was originally discovered,
more than a century ago,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.800
in faba beans.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.040
Might eating faba beans
help with Parkinson’s?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.600
I’ll explore just that question, next.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.720
Increased risk of Parkinson’s
disease has been associated

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.640
with exposure to pesticides,
consumption of dairy products,

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.680
a history of melanoma,
and traumatic brain injury.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.280
Why is the risk of Parkinson’s
disease increased among

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.560
individuals with high milk
and dairy consumption?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.400
It could be the animal fat.
Maybe the animal protein.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.360
So why not a plant-food
diet for the risk

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.400
and management of
Parkinson’s Disease?

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:32.080
There are phytochemicals that
may target the underlying cause,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.440
but in terms of treatment,
ancient sacred texts from

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.800
thousands of years ago refer to
trembling individuals who were

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.960
prescribed a plant from the
bean family to treat the condition.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:46.240
In my last video I talked
about the use of velvet beans,

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.360
but in 1913 the miracle drug L-dopa
was discovered for the first time,

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:56.480
in faba beans, also known
as fava beans or broad beans,

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.680
as a natural source of
L-dopa to consider.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.880
The amount varies considerably
based on a number of factors,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.360
but typically it looks like
they have about 10 times less

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.040
than velvet beans, but that’s okay
since you can eat larger quantities

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.280
since fava beans are an actual food
instead of a powdered supplement.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.000
The important thing is that
amount of L-dopa in fava beans

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:20.320
is enough to be pharmacologically
active in Parkinson’s disease.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.040
In fact, there are some reports
indicating that Parkinson’s patients

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.600
might respond better to the beans

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.280
than to standard L-dopa
preparations in pill form.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.240
But anecdotal reports that
patients may gain benefit

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:35.680
from a broad bean rich
diet don’t cut it.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.600
What you have to do...

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.080
is put it to the test.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.480
Parkinson’s patients were
fed about one and a third cups

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.960
of cooked fava beans, and
during the next four hours

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.920
a substantial clinical
improvement was noted.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.160
In fact similar to the
improvement seen after receiving

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.320
the standard pharmacological
combination of L-dopa plus carbidopa,

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:57.360
the decarboxylase inhibitor drug
I talked about in the last video

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:00.080
that boosts L-dopa
levels in the brain.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.240
No surprise that there
was a similar effect

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:05.440
since they had very similar
L-dopa levels in the blood.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.200
In fact, half the time you could
hardly tell the beans from the drugs.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.800
How could there be the same levels

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.720
if the bean L-dopa lacked
the carbidopa booster drug.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.160
Because fava beans may not
only be a natural source of L-dopa,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.760
but a natural source of
the carbidopa booster too.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.000
So the consumption of fava
beans has the potential

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.720
to increase the levels of L-dopa
and carbidopa in the blood,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.520
with a marked improvement in
the muscle movement performance

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.240
of the patients with Parkinson
disease, without any side effects.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.400
In fact they work so well
you have to be careful

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.240
about abruptly stopping them.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.760
There’s a condition called
neuroleptic malignant-like syndrome

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.520
characterized by fever, rigidity,
all sorts of neurological problems,

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.400
muscle breakdown, altered
levels of consciousness,

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.760
which is usually precipitated
by an abrupt withdrawal

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:56.560
of the L-dopa drug, caused by
an acute dopamine-deﬁcient state.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:59.040
Well, you can see the same
thing if you’re treating

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.800
your Parkinson’s with fava beans

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.800
and then all of a
sudden you stop them.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.240
Ten days before hospital
admission, this poor guy’s garden

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.640
ran out of beans, leading to
a severe crippling rigidity.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.120
This case demonstrates
that alternative therapies

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.440
carry similar risks to
traditional agents,

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.480
because in this case they really
are the ultimate traditional agent.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.280
There are some downsides you
don’t see with the drug, though.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:26.640
Like fava-induced flatulence.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.520
You also have to be careful with
fava consumption if you’re on

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.400
MAO inhibitor drugs often
used as anti-depressants,

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.120
since there can be
drug interactions.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.960
And then there's the risk of a
condition known as favism.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:42.640
There's a genetic mutation that
occurs in about 1 in 20 people,

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.880
and at even higher rates
in those of African,

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.720
Asian, and Mediterranean descent,

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:51.280
in which people lack an enzyme
that’s necessary to detoxify

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:53.200
certain compounds
found in fava beans,

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.280
and without the enzyme
fava bean consumption

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:57.920
can cause your red
blood cells to rupture.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.520
Thankfully, genetic testing for
this mutation is widely available

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.560
and affordable, and so it seems
prudent to screen patients

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.560
with Parkinson’s for this favism,

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.080
what's called G6PD
deﬁciency mutation,

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.280
prior to putting them on
daily fava bean consumption.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.120
If you want to give
fava beans a try.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.960
fresh green fava beans have
significantly more L-dopa than dried,

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.040
so much so that dried fava beans

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.520
may not provide any
clinical benefits.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:26.960
Roasting and boiling removes
some or even all of the L-dopa,

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.440
though other studies have
found that about a half cup

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:33.440
of cooked favas contain
approximately 250 mg.

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:38.240
Sprouted favas may have the
most, increasing up until day 9,

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:42.000
by which time the indigestible
flatulence sugars may be eliminated,

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.120
offering another advantage
of fava bean sprouting.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.840
But you don’t know if
fava bean sprouts help...

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.720
until you put them to the test.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.360
Researchers fed Parkinson’s
patients a salad with about

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.760
a half cup of freshly
chopped fava sprouts

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:01.600
and observed substantial
clinical improvement.

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.640
Other beans, just like
regular beans also naturally

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:07.040
have L-DOPA, though
at lower amounts.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:09.360
Soybeans have a bonus
compound that may act as

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.400
an L-dopa boosting
carbidopa compound.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.920
What if you fed
people soybeans

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.040
on top of their regular
Parkinson’s meds?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.520
Given people just one and a half
spoonful’s worth of roasted soybeans

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.640
led to a significant improvement
over the drugs alone

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:29.360
with significantly fewer involuntary
movements hours later.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.960
Until more information is available,
Parkinson’s combo drugs

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.680
like Sinemet should remain
the first-line therapy,

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:39.714
but adding beans to one’s
diet may only help.

